{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7KzcG52no7xCwEv9GwU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here's the draft, about 150 words:\n\n<final_document>\nSubject: Your own cleaner again, and $99 to come back\n\nHi,\n\nWhen customers left Brightway this past year, the two biggest reasons they gave us were price and a different cleaner showing up too often. You were right about the cleaners, and we've changed how we do it.\n\nSince July, every customer has their own regular cleaner, plus a named backup for sick days and holidays. You'll always know who's coming. Since we made that change, 1 of our 18 cleaners has left.\n\nAbout price: we cost more than the app services, and we can't match them. Our cleaners are employees, not contractors. We pay them $21 an hour and carry insurance on every visit. Most app services around here use contractors with no insurance on the visit.\n\nCome back and your first cleaning is $99. There's no contract and you can cancel any time. This offer ends December 31.\n\nTo book, reply to this email or call 555-0164.\n\nLisa Grant\nOwner, Brightway Home Cleaning\n</final_document>\n\nSome notes:\n\n- **The cleaner promise:** \"You'll always know who's coming\" is the strongest thing you can say truthfully. It's only true if customers are actually told their backup's name. Please make sure that happens before this goes out.\n- **Price after the first visit:** I left out $165 because you weren't sure what returning customers will pay. People will ask, so have an answer ready for replies and calls. If you settle on a price, add one line like \"After that, it's your regular rate of $X.\" It would also make the email stronger.\n- **Turnover:** \"1 of 18 since July\" is only about four months of data. It's true, so I kept it. Just don't round it up to something like \"our cleaners stay\" in replies.\n- **Greeting:** It says \"Hi,\" because you haven't decided on merging names. If you